  <div class="resource-section">
    <h3>Conversation Archives</h3>
    <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:0.75rem;">The AI conversation transcripts that produced this talk. These are the primary record of the intellectual work. Archives to be added as the ARK workflow is completed.</p>
    <ul class="resource-list">
      <li>
        <div>
          <span class="file-tag">arc</span>
          <span style="color:var(--muted);">Archives forthcoming</span>
          <div class="resource-desc">Conversation transcripts will be exported, styled, and added here via the ChatArchivist pipeline.</div>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="download-block">
    <h3>Download Everything</h3>
    <p>All materials in this repository — talk text, drafts, archives, and this page — are available as a single ZIP download from GitHub.</p>
    <p>On the repository page, click the green <code>Code</code> button and select <code>Download ZIP</code>.</p>
    <p>Repository: <code>stevesunypoly.github.io/tilde-steve/artifacts/</code></p>
  </div>

  <div class="resource-section">
    <h3>About This Work</h3>
    <p style="font-size:0.88rem;">This talk is part of a larger project developing AI literacy frameworks for the SUNY system in response to Board Resolution 2024-64, which mandates AI literacy integration into the Information Literacy general education competency across 64 campuses by Fall 2026.</p>
    <p style="font-size:0.88rem;">The framework is RTW: AI literacy as reading, thinking, and writing using the tools, techniques, and technological systems consistent with one's peers. Descriptive-analytical, not prescriptive. AI as cognitive infrastructure, not subject matter.</p>
    <p style="font-size:0.88rem;">The Learner's Permit, the credential stack, and related materials are available at the GitHub Pages site above.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="attribution">
    Steven M. Schneider · Professor, SUNY Polytechnic Institute · Co-Director, AIX Center<br>
    SUNY AI Fellow for the Public Good, 2025–2026<br>
    //steve.
  </div>
</div>

